# Line endings are normalised to LF everywhere, in the repository and in the
# working tree.
#
# Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows default — checks every
# text file out with CRLF endings. Prettier's `endOfLine` default is `lf`, so
# `pnpm format:check` then failed on 42 files that were byte-identical to their
# formatted output apart from carriage returns. That is a broken gate rather
# than a formatting backlog: it reported real problems and environmental noise
# in the same list, so the noise hid the one file (README.md) that genuinely
# needed reformatting.
#
# Running `prettier --write` across those files would have fixed nothing
# durably — the next checkout on a Windows machine would reintroduce every CRLF.
# Declaring the convention here fixes it for every contributor and every CI
# runner at once.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
